---
title: Quail with Grapes and Grappa
servings: 4 
source: http://www.myrecipes.com/recipe/quail-with-grapes-grappa-10000000522155/
tags: Poultry, Alcohol
---

@?fresh rosemary{}(optional) and @?fresh thyme{}(optional)

Cut 1/2 cup @seedless green grapes{1/2%cups} in half lengthwise.

Sprinkle @quail{8}(4oz. each, skinned) with @salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.
Place 1 @fresh rosemary{8%sprigs}(1" each) and @fresh thyme{8%sprigs}(1" each) into cavity of each quail.

Heat @olive oil{2%tsp} in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat.
Add quail; cook 3 minutes on each side or until browned.

Arrange quail, breast sides up, in pan; add @chicken broth{1/2%cup}(low-sodium).
Partially cover, reduce heat to medium-low, and cook ~{25%minutes} or until done.
Place quail on a platter; cover loosely with foil.

Add @chicken broth{1/4%cup}(low-sodium), @prosciutto{1%oz}(finely chopped),
@grappa{3%tbsp}(Italian brandy, or cognac), and @shallots{1 1/2%tbsp}(minced) to pan;
cook over medium-high heat 1 1/2 minutes or until shallots are tender, scraping pan to loosen browned bits.

Stir in @chicken broth{1/2%cup}(low-sodium), whole @seedless green grapes{1%cups}, and cut grapes;
cook 2 minutes or until grapes are thoroughly heated.

Pour grape mixture over quail; garnish with whole rosemary and thyme sprigs, if desired.
